# Native modules (better-sqlite3) must be compiled against Electron's
# bundled Node/V8 ABI, not whatever system Node happens to run `npm install`.
#
# Why: system Node can be much newer than Electron's bundled Node (e.g.
# system Node 26.x vs Electron 33's bundled Node ~20.x), and V8 removes
# APIs across versions (v8::Object::GetPrototype, v8::Context::GetIsolate,
# v8::PropertyCallbackInfo::This) that better-sqlite3's native addon still
# relies on. Building against a too-new system Node's headers fails
# outright at compile time -- it's not just a runtime ABI mismatch that
# scripts/rebuild-native.mjs can fix after the fact, because that script
# only runs from this project's own postinstall, which is never reached
# if better-sqlite3's own install script fails first.
#
# Setting these forces node-gyp / prebuild-install to target Electron's
# headers on the very first `npm install`, so the build succeeds directly
# instead of needing a separate rebuild step.
#
# `target` should track the resolved electron version (see the
# `allowScripts` key in package.json) -- it only needs to match the major
# Electron version (Node ABI is stable across an Electron major's patch
# releases), so it doesn't need updating on every patch bump.
runtime=electron
target=33.4.11
disturl=https://electronjs.org/headers
target_platform=darwin
